.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BN_MOD_INVERSE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BN_mod_inverse
.Nd compute inverse modulo n
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bn.h
.Ft BIGNUM *
.Fo BN_mod_inverse
.Fa "BIGNUM *r"
.Fa "BIGNUM *a"
.Fa "const BIGNUM *n"
.Fa "BN_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BN_mod_inverse
computes the inverse of
.Fa a
modulo
.Fa n
places the result in
.Fa r
.Pf ( Qo Li (a*r)%n==1 Qc Ns ).
If
.Fa r
is NULL, a new
.Vt BIGNUM
is created.
.Pp
.Fa ctx
is a previously allocated
.Vt BN_CTX
used for temporary variables.
.Fa r
may be the same
.Vt BIGNUM
as
.Fa a .
.Sh NOTES
It is an error to use the same
.Vt BIGNUM
as
.Fa n .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BN_mod_inverse
returns the
.Vt BIGNUM
containing the inverse, and NULL on error.
The error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr BN_add 3
